WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.200
Kicking off the week on Tesla's short time, daily, episode 495 for June 1st, 2026,

00:00:06.860 --> 00:00:11.620
I'm Patrick, coming to you from Vancouver. Let's see what the new week has in store for Tesla.

00:00:12.780 --> 00:00:17.000
European registration numbers for May landed with some real momentum behind them.

00:00:17.540 --> 00:00:24.740
Spain recorded 1,690 new Tesla registrations, which translated into a 112.8% increase

00:00:24.740 --> 00:00:29.800
compared with the same month last year. France posted an even steeper climate,

00:00:30.860 --> 00:00:38.060
655%, while Norway rose 29%, and Sweden reached 858 units for a 71% gain.

00:00:38.960 --> 00:00:43.120
Those figures extend a three-month stretch of improving results across the continent,

00:00:43.560 --> 00:00:48.260
and they arrived after a period when softer demand had raised questions about whether interest

00:00:48.260 --> 00:00:53.700
had faded for good. What stands out here is how quickly the picture shifted once pricing

00:00:53.700 --> 00:00:59.100
in inventory levels were adjusted, suggesting the earlier softness was more about availability

00:00:59.100 --> 00:01:05.580
and cost positioning than any lasting change in buyer appetite. Germany and Britain are still

00:01:05.580 --> 00:01:10.740
to report their own May numbers later this week, so the full regional picture will come into focus

00:01:10.740 --> 00:01:16.140
soon. If the pattern holds, it points to a market that can respond when Tesla fine-tunes its

00:01:16.140 --> 00:01:21.380
approach on price and stock rather than requiring a complete overhaul of the product lineup.

00:01:22.100 --> 00:01:27.600
That same flexibility shows up in how Tesla manages the materials that actually go into the cars.

00:01:28.000 --> 00:01:32.660
The company reached an agreement with Australian graphite supplier Sarah Resources

00:01:32.660 --> 00:01:38.220
that ends earlier threats to cancel the contract and locks in anode material flows needed for

00:01:38.220 --> 00:01:44.460
battery production. The resolution lifted Sarah shares more than 23% once the news broke.

00:01:44.980 --> 00:01:50.000
Securing those flows removes a near-term uncertainty from the supply chain at a moment when

00:01:50.000 --> 00:01:55.700
production schedules are already tight across multiple factories. It also underscores how critical

00:01:55.700 --> 00:02:01.080
long-term supplier relationships remain even when both sides have leveraged to walk away.

00:02:02.140 --> 00:02:08.620
Owners notice smaller refinements too. Tesla China rolled out an official manual retractable sunshade

00:02:08.620 --> 00:02:14.380
for the Model Y that matches the headliner fabric and carries side curtain airbag certification.

00:02:15.000 --> 00:02:19.460
The accessory directly tackles complaints about heat buildup in warmer climates and

00:02:19.460 --> 00:02:24.440
represents the first factory-backed solution of its kind for the refreshed Model Y.

00:02:25.120 --> 00:02:30.280
A related patent filing outlines work on an active shading system for large glass roofs

00:02:30.280 --> 00:02:33.800
that would cut cabin heat gain without adding meaningful weight.

00:02:34.480 --> 00:02:40.220
Those details matter because they show Tesla responding to real-world owner feedback on comfort

00:02:40.220 --> 00:02:46.740
without waiting for a full model redesign cycle. The sunshade is available now while the active system

00:02:46.740 --> 00:02:51.900
remains in development, but both reflect the same focus on incremental cabin improvements

00:02:51.900 --> 00:02:58.600
that owners actually feel during daily use. On the charging side, Volvo is extending access to

00:02:58.600 --> 00:03:04.600
Tesla superchargers for its drivers across Europe and the Asia-Pacific region. The move builds on

00:03:04.600 --> 00:03:09.840
earlier North American agreements and increases the number of non-Tesla vehicles that can use the

00:03:09.840 --> 00:03:16.540
network. For Tesla, each new partner adds utilization without requiring additional capital spending on

00:03:16.540 --> 00:03:23.020
new stalls. For Volvo owners, it means more reliable fast-charging options on longer trips where

00:03:23.020 --> 00:03:28.920
third-party networks may still have coverage gaps. At the same time, other manufacturers are bringing

00:03:28.920 --> 00:03:35.260
their own vehicles into the same segments Tesla occupies. BMW introduced the IX3 Electric SUV

00:03:35.820 --> 00:03:42.840
and refreshed versions of the X5 and X7. The IX3 is positioned squarely against the Model Y in both

00:03:42.840 --> 00:03:48.600
Europe and North America, with updated styling and new power trains also appearing on the larger

00:03:48.600 --> 00:03:55.200
X models. Pricing and production timing details are expected later this year. The launch serves as a

00:03:55.200 --> 00:04:01.620
reminder that legacy automakers continue to target the same premium electric SUV buyers Tesla has

00:04:01.620 --> 00:04:07.260
cultivated, and the competitive pressure will likely intensify once those vehicles reach showrooms

00:04:07.260 --> 00:04:13.360
in volume. Resale dynamics have created a sharper contrast for one vehicle in particular.

00:04:13.980 --> 00:04:20.120
Early Cybertruck reservation holders who pay the original $150,000 foundation series price

00:04:20.120 --> 00:04:27.040
are now seeing steep depreciation after repeated MSRP reductions widen the gap between launch pricing

00:04:27.040 --> 00:04:32.520
and current transaction levels. Later buyers gain from the lower entry points, yet the largest

00:04:32.520 --> 00:04:38.500
adjustment has fallen on those who took delivery first. The situation illustrates how aggressive price

00:04:38.500 --> 00:04:44.260
cuts, while helpful for new demand, can create short-term pain for the earliest adopters in a still

00:04:44.260 --> 00:04:50.600
maturing market segment. Safety performance under extreme conditions offers a different angle.

00:04:51.120 --> 00:04:58.020
A Model 3 that went over a 300-foot cliff in Malibu left both occupants alive, with the vehicle's

00:04:58.020 --> 00:05:04.220
structural integrity and restraint systems performing as designed. Tesla noted the outcome as another

00:05:04.220 --> 00:05:10.700
real-world example of occupant protection. Stories like this sit alongside ongoing conversations about

00:05:10.700 --> 00:05:16.420
how the company describes the capabilities of its driver assistance systems, and they reinforce that

00:05:16.420 --> 00:05:21.700
the hardware itself continues to demonstrate resilience when tested in ways no one plans for.

00:05:22.680 --> 00:05:27.420
Taking a step back, the European registration rebound challenges the idea that demand

00:05:27.420 --> 00:05:35.040
weakness on the continent was baked into the market structure. Spain's 112.8% year-over-year increase,

00:05:35.460 --> 00:05:41.680
alongside the gains in France, Sweden, and Norway, followed several months of softer results and arrived

00:05:41.680 --> 00:05:47.140
after Tesla adjusted pricing and availability. The three consecutive months of growth suggest

00:05:47.140 --> 00:05:53.060
external factors such as cost and inventory played larger roles than some observers had assumed.

00:05:53.620 --> 00:05:58.580
That pattern fits with Tesla's vertical integration model, where control over software,

00:05:58.940 --> 00:06:03.360
pricing, and allocation lets the company shift resources across regions faster than

00:06:03.360 --> 00:06:08.680
competitors tied to longer production cycles or dealer networks. Whether the recovery proves

00:06:08.680 --> 00:06:13.840
durable will depend on the next several months of data, especially once a Britain and Germany report.

00:06:14.400 --> 00:06:20.040
Those upcoming figures should clarify if the recent uptake reflects a lasting rebalancing or simply

00:06:20.040 --> 00:06:26.660
an inventory-driven spike. Meanwhile, the supply chain agreement with SIRA and the Model Y Sunshade

00:06:26.660 --> 00:06:31.960
both point to steady behind-the-scenes work that keeps production moving and addresses daily owner

00:06:31.960 --> 00:06:39.180
concerns. The Volvo network access and BMW product launches show the charging ecosystem and competitive

00:06:39.180 --> 00:06:45.120
field evolving in parallel, and the contrast between early cyber truck depreciation and the Model

00:06:45.120 --> 00:06:51.400
3 survival story reminds us that market pricing and physical safety operate on entirely different

00:06:51.400 --> 00:06:57.440
timelines. Tomorrow we'll be watching for the Britain and Germany registration figures to see whether

00:06:57.440 --> 00:07:05.580
the European rebound holds. That's your Tesla news for today. TSLA closed at $423.33

00:07:06.160 --> 00:07:14.680
down $12.46, 2.9%. If you found this useful, a rating or review on Apple podcasts or Spotify

00:07:14.680 --> 00:07:20.580
really helps new listeners find the show. You can also find us on X at Tesla Shorts Time.

00:07:21.040 --> 00:07:25.600
I'm Patrick in Vancouver. Thanks for listening and I'll see you tomorrow. And before you go,

